    "topic": "Network Mocking & Error State Injection via page.route()",
    "question": "How do you intercept third-party payment gateway or analytics APIs in Playwright using page.route(), and how do you simulate 500 Internal Server Errors and slow 3G network latency without relying on external sandbox backends?",
    "expectedFocus": "page.route() interception, route.fulfill() with mock JSON, route.abort(), simulating latency with route.continue() or delayed fulfill, eliminating third-party flakiness.",
    "answerSummary": "### 1. Conceptual Breakdown (Plain English)\n**What it is:** Use page.\n**Why it matters in QA:** Understanding this concept enables QA engineers to bridge the gap between business specifications and technical verification, eliminating guesswork and test flakiness.\n\n### 2. Deep-Dive Technical Explanation\nUse page.route() to intercept matching network patterns. Call route.fulfill({ status: 500, contentType: \"application/json\", body: JSON.stringify({ error: \"Gateway Timeout\" }) }) to verify client error handling. To test latency or slow connections, inject a delay before fulfilling or modify network emulation via CDP.\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Practical Application Guide\n• **Step 1: Identify Preconditions & Scope:** Clarify the exact system boundary, inputs, and expected environmental states before executing.\n• **Step 2: Construct Deterministic Assertions:** Avoid relying on arbitrary delays; instead, assert against explicit system state transitions and verifiable outcomes.\n• **Step 3: Isolate Environmental Variables:** Ensure test data is cleanly provisioned and cleaned up so parallel or subsequent runs remain independent.\n\n### 4. Key Terminology for QA Engineers\n• **Deterministic Testing:** A testing approach where a given input always produces the exact same observable outcome without intermittent or random failures.\n• **Flakiness (Flaky Test):** A test that intermittently passes and fails on identical application builds without any code changes, usually caused by timing race conditions or shared mutable state.\n• **Quality Gate:** An automated checkpoint in the CI/CD pipeline that blocks flawed builds from progressing to staging or production.",
    "codeSnippet": "// Mock failed payment gateway response in Playwright\nawait page.route('**/api/v1/checkout/pay', async route => {\n  await route.fulfill({\n    status: 500,\n    contentType: 'application/json',\n    body: JSON.stringify({ error: 'CardProcessorDeclined' })\n  });\n});\nawait page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit Payment' }).click();\nawait expect(page.getByText('Payment failed. Please try again.')).toBeVisible();",
    "bestPractice": "Mock flaky external 3rd-party services (Stripe, Twilio, Google Analytics) to keep CI deterministic and avoid burning live sandbox quotas.",
    "pitfallToAvoid": "Hitting real production third-party APIs during automated test runs, which introduces flakiness and security token leakage."
